Theorem CH-106: fixpoint engine bootstrap (IC-7 SCC convergence on 2-function call graph)

  Preconditions:
    - G is a synthetic 2-function call graph per Annex E §AIMS IC-1 with two functions f and g and a single edge
      f calls g; G has one SCC of size 1 for each function (no
      recursion); topological order processes g before f per IC-1
    - the AimsState dimension under analysis is Access x Consumption
      per Annex E §AIMS.1 + sec-1.2 (height 1 + height 3 =
      lattice height 4)
    - IC-7 convergence bound per the rule's authoritative formula:
      param_count * 13 + 8 + 6 + 4 (the per-domain heights summed);
      restricted to the sub-lattice and a 1-param function, the
      bound is 1 * 4 + 0 + 0 + 0 = 4 iterations
    - fixpoint engine consumes bounded iteration with explicit
      termination witness and per-iteration progress measure per
      the foundational-axiom policy sec-Per-Engine-Constructive-Proof-Shape

  Soundness property:
    Forall G in synthetic 2-function call graphs over the
    Access x Consumption sub-lattice.
      the SCC fixpoint over G converges in at most 4 iterations;
      the converged ParamContract for f is the LUB of the per-call-site
      contracts at the f-to-g edge, restricted to the sub-lattice;
      the convergence is constructive (per L-5 finite-height + IC-7
      iteration bound).

  Proof obligation:
    Bounded iteration argument with explicit termination witness.

      Setup:
        Let the SCC fixpoint maintain a per-function ParamContract
        for f and for g, each restricted to the Access x Consumption
        sub-lattice. Initial values per IC-2 are the most-optimistic
        (Borrowed, Dead) on the sub-lattice.

      Iteration trace (worst case):
        Iteration 0 (initialization):
          ParamContract(f) = (Borrowed, Dead); ParamContract(g) = (Borrowed, Dead).
        Iteration 1 (process g first per IC-1 topological order):
          g's body has no callees; ParamContract(g) is updated by
          processing g's body; per IC-3 the join over g's call sites
          (none in this scaffold-time fixpoint) leaves ParamContract(g)
          at (Borrowed, Dead).
          Process f: f calls g once; the call site joins f's argument
          state into ParamContract(g) per IC-3.
          ParamContract(g) widens from (Borrowed, Dead) toward the
          argument state; suppose argument is (Owned, Linear); the
          join produces (max(Borrowed, Owned), max(Dead, Linear)) =
          (Owned, Linear).
        Iteration 2:
          Re-process g: still no callees; ParamContract(g) stable
          at (Owned, Linear).
          Re-process f: f's argument state may have widened if f
          consumes g's contract; one more pass at most produces a
          single componentwise widening step.
        Iteration 3:
          Same as iteration 2 with no further widening; the
          fixpoint is reached.
        Iteration 4 (bound):
          Iteration 3's output equals iteration 2's output; the
          convergence check succeeds.

    Progress measure:
      Define progress(it) = sum over dimensions of the height of
      the current contract value on that dimension. Per L-5 the
      sub-lattice has finite height (Access = 1 plus Consumption
      = 3 = 4). Progress is monotone non-decreasing across
      iterations (per L-6 monotonicity of the join). The progress
      measure is bounded above by 4 (the sub-lattice height).
      Therefore the fixpoint terminates after at most 4 iterations.

    Termination witness:
      The iteration limit per IC-7 (param_count * 13 plus the
      domain-heights) bounds the convergence; restricted to one
      parameter and the Access x Consumption sub-lattice the
      effective bound is 4 iterations. Beyond iteration 4, the
      analysis emits a diagnostic per IC-7's "abort with diagnostic"
      clause; this scaffold-time bootstrap proof exhibits
      convergence at iteration 3 (one iteration below the bound).

    Lattice validation:
      L-5 (finite height per dimension) is the substrate for the
      fixpoint termination argument. L-6 (transfer-function
      monotonicity) ensures progress is non-decreasing. IC-3's
      componentwise join is monotone over the partial order on
      ParamContract per the sub-lattice's componentwise ordering.

    Engines dispatched:
      fixpoint (bounded iteration; explicit termination witness;
                per-iteration progress measure; IC-7 convergence
                bound discharge)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: 01A bootstrap discharged via §01A Implementation Items (engine constructive verification + Lean 4 cross-validation)
